hat has been approved months in advance by a specialist IT group.","position":{"start":{"line":32,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"key":"nGKXIoFFHm"}],"key":"gEGZTYyHuX"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":34,"column":1},"end":{"line":34,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In recent weeks lectures at schools and universities around the world have moved to on-line classrooms and one shortcoming of binder has become apparent — the lack of persistence for work that spans an extended work session. The fact that students (and lecturers) working at home may be forced to work in a fragmented fashion means that they often time-out access in binder and have to restart a new, pristine session each time they return.","position":{"start":{"line":34,"column":1},"end":{"line":34,"column":1}},"key":"aqnYx8OFUC"}],"key":"wqi7sshOXB"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We built a cheap-and-cheerful solution with persistent storage and a binder-like access to notebooks in a repository that is aimed at serving a single classroom. We provide a template github repository that can be used to configure, manage and monitor a single ","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"Z5kYIfdMua"},{"type":"link","url":"/articles/underworld/www.digitalocean.com","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"digital-ocean","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"VxvLbkSC4L"}],"urlSource":"/articles/underworld/www.digitalocean.com","key":"dGhwvLNhh7"},{"type":"text","value":" droplet (any server, really) that serves up content via* ","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"TTnOWFtZBu"},{"type":"link","url":"http://tljh.jupyter.org/en/latest/","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line